d LiF tracer-diffusion or ionic-conductivity Arrhenius data. (b) Li self-diffusion in molten LiF above its melting point, a well-defined MD observable; validate first by recovering LiF's measured melting point or liquid density with the same model.\"}\nEOF\n./board post run_report @/tmp/refusal.json --parent 29a041b9-af2f-4735-b1d4-f6f0b0843735","description":"Post refusal run_report to board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":763,"cache_read_input_tokens":32509,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":763,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebfbebb7-f853-4d55-ad8c-9f5e1740791f","uuid":"bcde71d3-85f0-4f95-b4b7-454d0e7c26c1","timestamp":"2026-11-01T03:56:46.140Z","request_id":"req_011CgbY12LhAK4hM8ugr7rhk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QyscsYHCztLuSgK2BaVjh8":{"command":"cd /work && cat > /tmp/refusal.json <<'EOF'\n{\"status\": \"refused\",\n \"task\": \"Li-ion self_diffusion (cm2/s) in pristine crystalline LiF by molecular dynamics\",\n \"reason\": \"PREMISE CHECK FAILED. (1) Ill-posed for a pristine crystal: in defect-free rock-salt LiF below melting, Li+ only vibrates about lattice sites; measurable Li diffusion in LiF is vacancy-mediated (thermal Schottky pairs or extrinsic/impurity vacancies), so it depends on defect concentration, which a pristine cell sets to zero by construction. (2) Not measurable at MD scale: equilibrium vacancy fractions in the solid are far below 1/N_atoms for any affordable cell (1e3-1e4 atoms), and vacancy hops are rare events on ns timescales. A perfect-cell MLIP MD run would give a plateaued MSD and 'D ~ 0 within resolution'. That number is an artifact of cell size and run length, not a property of LiF. Gettin